  "body": "From #71. The robust axis fit sets small off-centre features aside, but it runs after the existing gate: if off-axis features make up more than ~10% of the surface (OK_SHARE 90%) or drag the plain fit past the 0.3 mm tolerance, the part is refused as not revolved before the robust pass sees it - e.g. a 20 mm keyway with a deep floor. Safe (a refusal), but such parts can't be turned.\n\nDone means: the robust consensus runs before the concurrency gate (or the gate is read on the kept set), so a revolved part with a large keyway/flat fits and passes; the untrusted-fit refusal text gets a test.",
